      },
      "message": "feat(tools): draw a milling tool's cutter, neck and shank as a spun profile\n\n#93 slice 2 (slice 1, the drawn holder, was #475). A milling tool's own\nshape is now a drawn spun half-outline beside its numbers:\n\n- camcraft-tools cutter_profile: the agreement law - refused by name when\n  the outline is no spun profile, is on a turning tool, leaves the tip,\n  is not exactly the stated diameter within the flutes, does not end at\n  flute + shank length, is wider than the stated shank above the flutes,\n  or folds over itself; parametric() is the numbers' own outline.\n- schema::ToolCutter + app::tool_cutter (display only: no generator or\n  law reads it; a drawn cutter moves no operation stamp).\n- SetToolCutter, one undo step; ChangeTool refuses a number edit that\n  would break a drawn cutter; DeleteTool / DeleteEntity restore it.\n- MCP get_tool_cutter_profile / set_tool_cutter_profile.\n- Project: additive `cutter` key on the tool record, no version step.\n- Tool editor Profile tab: Draw holder / Draw cutter, Parametric /\n  Custom, the shared flat side view, live refusal, Apply cutter.\n\nRefs #93\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
